{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RpT3GqfUbLm6ivWBSe2hi5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-543\"\n3\ttitle = \"SR-163's owner: the tolerant requirement-reference cell, the four-class checker warn-first, the direct TC (OI-72)\"\n4\tspecref = \"\"\n5\tworkstream = \"requirements\"\n6\tsr_refs = [\"SR-163\"]\n7\tneeds = []\n8\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n9\tsafety_class = \"spine\"\n10\tpriority = 3\n11\t+++\n12\t\n13\t## Deliverable\n14\t\n15\tSR-163's verification shipped mechanism-first, all four done-when met:\n16\t\n17\t1. **The tolerant cell** — `bootstrap.py::MAPPING` rows may carry a requirement\n18\t   reference as an optional third element; `bootstrap.mapping_entries()`\n19\t   normalizes every row to `(src, dst, ref|None)`, so a bare pair keeps working\n20\t   (by definition an unmapped-entry warning) with no flag day — the burn-down IS\n21\t   the migration. Every consumer (the copy pass, the dogfood walk, the kit-path\n22\t   invariant, the resync/profile tests) unpacks pairs and triples.\n23\t2. **The four-class checker** lands in `gen_arch_map.py` (LLR-204's module, the\n24\t   purpose-reference home) beside the back-link machinery:\n25\t   `mapping_purpose_findings` returns the four classes, `resolve_requirement_reference`\n26\t   is the SR → live-stakeholder-need join stated once, `load_spine_index` loads\n27\t   the repo's SR/SN registries, `mapping_purpose_report` computes the pass, and\n28\t   `MAPPING_FINDING_POLICY` is the one warn-vs-gate home (unmapped/unresolved\n29\t   WARN; missing/stale GATE — already delivered/zero via the dogfood+bootstrap\n30\t   checks). The stale arm honors the `LIFECYCLE:` marker the dogfood walk applies.\n31\t   The flip of a warn class to gate at count zero is a later reviewed commit.\n32\t3. **The direct TC on SR-163** — TC-204 (`tests/test_mapping_purpose.py`, Smoke\n33\t   tier, registered Drafted; approving it is the owner's act) plants one defect\n34\t   of each class on a synthetic scaffold plus a clean control and asserts each is\n35\t   reported, drives the checker over the real `bootstrap.MAPPING` + this repo's\n36\t   real spine and asserts no gate-class finding survives and every filled\n37\t   reference resolves — so the TC claims exactly what it exercises.\n38\t4. **The burn-down begun, not finished** — 20 references filled to unambiguous\n39\t   EXISTING SRs; no new SR needed (no filled file lacked a justifying\n40\t   requirement). **Baseline for the burn-down:** of 147 MAPPING rows, 20 carry a\n41\t   resolved reference and **127 remain bare** (unmapped_file WARN); 0 unresolved,\n42\t   0 missing, 0 stale over the real inventory. The 127 is the count the burn-down\n43\t   retires against; gating flips only at zero, per the ruling.\n44\t\n45\tHarness kept green: the module-size ratchet (`bootstrap.py` +29 SLOC,\n46\t`gen_arch_map.py` +79 SLOC) and the smoke membership budget (max-tests 1440 →\n47\t1458, +17 in-process TC-204 tests) re-stamped as reviewed baseline edits naming\n48\tthis WI. No new LLR, no new `stack.ini` step (`bootstrap.py` never ships\n49\tdownstream, so the kit self-check home is TC-204, which runs the checker over\n50\tthe real inventory on every suite run). Full design record in\n51\t`docs/log.d/WI-543-sr163-verification-tc.md`.\n52\t\n53\t## Context\n54\t\n55\tRE-SCOPED 2026-08-31 by `OI-72`'s ruling (record\n56\t`docs/log.d/2026-08-31-owner-rulings-oi70-71-72.md`, compiled into\n57\t`docs/log.md`), which also names this row `SR-163`'s OWNING row. The original\n58\tscope — author the whole file→requirement→need join before anything counts —\n59\tis replaced by mechanism-first: `SR-163`'s own text puts the warn-to-gate\n60\tdial in the requirement, so the honest minimal build ships the mechanism, a\n61\tdirect TC that claims exactly what it exercises, and the reference authoring\n62\tas a visible warn-count burn-down rather than a precondition.\n63\t\n64\tThe state this row inherits: `SR-163` (Approved, `verification = \"Test\"`)\n65\tnames four finding classes. Missing files and stale entries are delivered\n66\t(the dogfood walk and bootstrap checks — `TC-199`/`TC-200`'s evidence, rows\n67\tDrafted on the wi508 branch until `WI-555` lands them). UNRESOLVED REFERENCE\n68\tand UNMAPPED FILE cannot occur because `bootstrap.py::MAPPING` — the declared\n69\tinventory — is source→destination pairs with no place to record WHY a file\n70\tships (the undischarged arm `LLR-203` records on-row).\n71\t\n72\t## Done-when\n73\t\n74\t1. **The tolerant cell:** a MAPPING row may carry a requirement reference as\n75\t   a third element; the reader accepts both pairs and triples — a bare pair\n76\t   is by definition an unmapped-entry WARNING, so downstream inventories keep\n77\t   working with no flag day and the burn-down IS the migration.\n78\t2. **The checker**, over the real inventory on every run: each reference\n79\t   resolves SR → stakeholder need, each destination exists, every bare pair\n80\t   is named; a generated output maps through its generator's row; the\n81\t   declared policy assigns warn versus gate per class — unresolved and\n82\t   unmapped start WARN here and the SHIPPED default for unmapped stays\n83\t   warn-only (ruled); the flip to gating is a reviewed commit at count zero.\n84\t3. **The direct TC on `SR-163`** proves the CHECKER catches each of the four\n85\t   classes on a scaffold (remove a file; plant a bogus reference; leave a\n86\t   bare pair; a stale entry) — the checker's green over the real MAPPING is\n87\t   the standing every-file-maps evidence, so the TC claims exactly what it\n88\t   exercises. Spine rows through the ordinary approval flow under the\n89\t   declared dial.\n90\t4. **The burn-down begun, not finished:** references filled where the\n91\t   justifying SR is unambiguous (most cite EXISTING SRs; a new SR is minted\n92\t   only where a shipped file has no justifying requirement — surfacing those\n93\t   is the point, per SN-038); the remaining warn count recorded in the close\n94\t   fragment as the baseline the burn-down retires against.\n95\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"702ff475-900d-498d-8b02-faadfbdec2de","uuid":"71877a1f-f7b8-4348-ac0d-3c927a36334c","timestamp":"2026-09-01T04:55:46.697Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-543-sr163-verification-tc/docs/work/active/wi-543-sr163-verification-tc/WI-543-sr163-verification-tc.md","content":"+++\nid = \"WI-543\"\ntitle = \"SR-163's owner: the tolerant requirement-reference cell, the four-class checker warn-first, the direct TC (OI-72)\"\nspecref = \"\"\nworkstream = \"requirements\"\nsr_refs = [\"SR-163\"]\nneeds = []\nbuildtier = \"strong\"\nsafety_class = \"spine\"\npriority = 3\n+++\n\n## Deliverable\n\nSR-163's verification shipped mechanism-first, all four done-when met:\n\n1. **The tolerant cell** — `bootstrap.py::MAPPING` rows may carry a requirement\n   reference as an optional third element; `bootstrap.mapping_entries()`\n   normalizes every row to `(src, dst, ref|None)`, so a bare pair keeps working\n   (by definition an unmapped-entry warning) with no flag day — the burn-down IS\n   the migration. Every consumer (the copy pass, the dogfood walk, the kit-path\n   invariant, the resync/profile tests) unpacks pairs and triples.\n2. **The four-class checker** lands in `gen_arch_map.py` (LLR-204's module, the\n   purpose-reference home) beside the back-link machinery:\n   `mapping_purpose_findings` returns the four classes, `resolve_requirement_reference`\n   is the SR → live-stakeholder-need join stated once, `load_spine_index` loads\n   the repo's SR/SN registries, `mapping_purpose_report` computes the pass, and\n   `MAPPING_FINDING_POLICY` is the one warn-vs-gate home (unmapped/unresolved\n   WARN; missing/stale GATE — already delivered/zero via the dogfood+bootstrap\n   checks). The stale arm honors the `LIFECYCLE:` marker the dogfood walk applies.\n   The flip of a warn class to gate at count zero is a later reviewed commit.\n3. **The direct TC on SR-163** — TC-204 (`tests/test_mapping_purpose.py`, Smoke\n   tier, registered Drafted; approving it is the owner's act) plants one defect\n   of each class on a synthetic scaffold plus a clean control and asserts each is\n   reported, drives the checker over the real `bootstrap.MAPPING` + this repo's\n   real spine and asserts no gate-class finding survives and every filled\n   reference resolves — so the TC claims exactly what it exercises.\n4. **The burn-down begun, not finished** — 20 references filled to unambiguous\n   EXISTING SRs; no new SR needed (no filled file lacked a justifying\n   requirement). **Baseline for the burn-down:** of 147 MAPPING rows, 20 carry a\n   resolved reference and **127 remain bare** (unmapped_file WARN); 0 unresolved,\n   0 missing, 0 stale over the real inventory. The 127 is the count the burn-down\n   retires against; gating flips only at zero, per the ruling.\n\nHarness kept green: the module-size ratchet (`bootstrap.py` +29 SLOC,\n`gen_arch_map.py` +79 SLOC) and the smoke membership budget (max-tests 1440 →\n1458, +17 in-process TC-204 tests) re-stamped as reviewed baseline edits naming\nthis WI. No new LLR, no new `stack.ini` step (`bootstrap.py` never ships\ndownstream, so the kit self-check home is TC-204, which runs the checker over\nthe real inventory on every suite run). Full design record in\n`docs/log.d/WI-543-sr163-verification-tc.md`.\n\n## Context\n\nRE-SCOPED 2026-08-31 by `OI-72`'s ruling (record\n`docs/log.d/2026-08-31-owner-rulings-oi70-71-72.md`, compiled into\n`docs/log.md`), which also names this row `SR-163`'s OWNING row. The original\nscope — author the whole file→requirement→need join before anything counts —\nis replaced by mechanism-first: `SR-163`'s own text puts the warn-to-gate\ndial in the requirement, so the honest minimal build ships the mechanism, a\ndirect TC that claims exactly what it exercises, and the reference authoring\nas a visible warn-count burn-down rather than a precondition.\n\nThe state this row inherits: `SR-163` (Approved, `verification = \"Test\"`)\nnames four finding classes. Missing files and stale entries are delivered\n(the dogfood walk and bootstrap checks — `TC-199`/`TC-200`'s evidence, rows\nDrafted on the wi508 branch until `WI-555` lands them). UNRESOLVED REFERENCE\nand UNMAPPED FILE cannot occur because `bootstrap.py::MAPPING` — the declared\ninventory — is source→destination pairs with no place to record WHY a file\nships (the undischarged arm `LLR-203` records on-row).\n\n## Done-when\n\n1. **The tolerant cell:** a MAPPING row may carry a requirement reference as\n   a third element; the reader accepts both pairs and triples — a bare pair\n   is by definition an unmapped-entry WARNING, so downstream inventories keep\n   working with no flag day and the burn-down IS the migration.\n2. **The checker**, over the real inventory on every run: each reference\n   resolves SR → stakeholder need, each destination exists, every bare pair\n   is named; a generated output maps through its generator's row; the\n   declared policy assigns warn versus gate per class — unresolved and\n   unmapped start WARN here and the SHIPPED default for unmapped stays\n   warn-only (ruled); the flip to gating is a reviewed commit at count zero.\n3. **The direct TC on `SR-163`** proves the CHECKER catches each of the four\n   classes on a scaffold (remove a file; plant a bogus reference; leave a\n   bare pair; a stale entry) — the checker's green over the real MAPPING is\n   the standing every-file-maps evidence, so the TC claims exactly what it\n   exercises. Spine rows through the ordinary approval flow under the\n   declared dial.\n4. **The burn-down begun, not finished:** references filled where the\n   justifying SR is unambiguous (most cite EXISTING SRs; a new SR is minted\n   only where a shipped file has no justifying requirement — surfacing