{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XKQs6HTJL1QU8VSUiBM1xk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## 2026-08-31 — WI-543: SR-163's owner — the tolerant reference cell, the four-class checker warn-first, the direct TC (OI-72)\n2\t\n3\tRe-scoped row per `OI-72`'s ruling (log.md 2026-08-31). SR-163's verification is\n4\tmechanism-first: ship the tolerant `MAPPING` reference cell, a checker that runs\n5\tthe four finding classes over the real inventory, and a direct TC on SR-163 that\n6\tproves the checker catches each class on a scaffold — with the reference\n7\tburn-down begun, not finished.\n8\t\n9\t### Build\n10\t\n11\t1. **Tolerant cell** — `bootstrap.py::MAPPING` rows may carry a requirement\n12\t   reference as an optional third element; `bootstrap.mapping_entries()`\n13\t   normalizes every row to `(src, dst, ref|None)` so a bare pair keeps working\n14\t   and is by definition an unmapped-entry warning. All consumers (the copy pass,\n15\t   the dogfood walk, the kit-path invariant, the resync/profile tests) unpack\n16\t   pairs and triples.\n17\t2. **The checker** — in `gen_arch_map.py` (LLR-204's module, the purpose-\n18\t   reference home), the forward direction beside the backlink machinery:\n19\t   `mapping_purpose_findings(entries, present, sr_by_id, sn_ids,\n20\t   declared_absences)` returns the four classes; `resolve_requirement_reference`\n21\t   is the SR → live-stakeholder-need join stated once; `load_spine_index` loads\n22\t   the repo's SR/SN registries; `mapping_purpose_report` computes the pass.\n23\t   `MAPPING_FINDING_POLICY` is the one home for warn-vs-gate: `unmapped_file` and\n24\t   `unresolved_reference` WARN, `missing_file` and `stale_entry` GATE (they are\n25\t   already delivered/zero via the dogfood+bootstrap checks). The stale arm\n26\t   honors the `LIFECYCLE:` marker, the same rule the dogfood walk applies. The\n27\t   flip of a warn class to gate at count zero is a later reviewed commit.\n28\t3. **The direct TC on SR-163** — TC-204 (`tests/test_mapping_purpose.py`, Smoke\n29\t   tier so it runs on every commit bar): plants one defect of each class on a\n30\t   synthetic scaffold plus a clean control and asserts each is reported; drives\n31\t   the checker over the real `bootstrap.MAPPING` + this repo's real spine and\n32\t   asserts NO gate-class finding survives (the standing every-file-maps\n33\t   evidence) and every filled reference resolves. Registered Drafted (SR-163 is\n34\t   Approved; approving TC-204 is the owner's act).\n35\t4. **Burn-down begun** — 20 references filled to unambiguous EXISTING SRs\n36\t   (`SR-049` derived stage, `SR-137` one policy home, `SR-146` prompts ×9,\n37\t   `SR-147` spine registries ×3, `SR-159` interfaces ×2, `SR-015` perf budgets,\n38\t   `SR-151` hosted CI, `SR-161` hats). No new SR needed yet — no filled file\n39\t   lacked a justifying requirement.\n40\t\n41\t**Baseline (recorded for the burn-down):** of 147 MAPPING rows, 20 carry a\n42\tresolved reference and **127 remain bare (unmapped_file WARN)**; 0 unresolved, 0\n43\tmissing, 0 stale over the real inventory. The 127 is the count the burn-down\n44\tretires against; gating flips only at zero, per the ruling.\n45\t\n46\t### Design notes\n47\t\n48\t- No new LLR: the ruling keeps the wi508 rows (LLR-203/204, TC-199/200) as they\n49\t  are and makes TC-204 a DIRECT test on SR-163. The checker's functions carry no\n50\t  `Implements:` tag / LLR — back-link coverage is warn-only, and the mechanism\n51\t  is verified by its direct TC.\n52\t- No new `stack.ini` step: `bootstrap.py` is excluded from its own MAPPING and\n53\t  never ships downstream, so a harness step over `bootstrap.MAPPING` would be\n54\t  dead in every adopter. The kit self-check home is the test, which runs the\n55\t  checker over the real inventory on every suite run — the \"on every run\"\n56\t  evidence the ruling asks for. An adopter with their own inventory can call the\n57\t  `gen_arch_map` functions directly.\n58\t\n59\t### Close\n60\t\n61\t- **Harness re-stamps (reviewed baseline edits naming this WI):** the checker's\n62\t  new behavior grew two ratcheted modules past baseline — `bootstrap.py` +29\n63\t  SLOC (1571 → 1600, the tolerant cell) and `gen_arch_map.py` +79 SLOC (1262 →\n64\t  1341, the four-class checker) — both re-stamped UP in `tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py`\n65\t  as reviewed bumps, not monolith drift (the placement is LLR-204's module by\n66\t  the ruling; decomposition remains WI-521's program). TC-204's 17 in-process\n67\t  smoke tests pushed the smoke tier to 1450 collected, so `docs/stack.ini`\n68\t  `[smoke-budget] max-tests` re-stamped 1440 → 1458 (+8 headroom, the standing\n69\t  small-slack posture); the seconds budget is NOT touched (smoke wall 21.8 s vs\n70\t  60 s).\n71\t- **Approval brief regenerated** (`trace.py --approve modified`): TC-204 (the\n72\t  one spine row this WI minted, Drafted) now appears in `docs/ratify/CURRENT.md`\n73\t  as ADDED-since-snapshot / never-approved — approving it is the owner's act.\n74\t- **Verification:** commit bar green (smoke + budget enforce); the full\n75\t  unfiltered suite run to green before close.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"702ff475-900d-498d-8b02-faadfbdec2de","uuid":"7f6c5827-5a63-451e-994a-14c0fb694d1f","timestamp":"2026-09-01T04:55:46.972Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-543-sr163-verification-tc/docs/log.d/WI-543-sr163-verification-tc.md","content":"## 2026-08-31 — WI-543: SR-163's owner — the tolerant reference cell, the four-class checker warn-first, the direct TC (OI-72)\n\nRe-scoped row per `OI-72`'s ruling (log.md 2026-08-31). SR-163's verification is\nmechanism-first: ship the tolerant `MAPPING` reference cell, a checker that runs\nthe four finding classes over the real inventory, and a direct TC on SR-163 that\nproves the checker catches each class on a scaffold — with the reference\nburn-down begun, not finished.\n\n### Build\n\n1. **Tolerant cell** — `bootstrap.py::MAPPING` rows may carry a requirement\n   reference as an optional third element; `bootstrap.mapping_entries()`\n   normalizes every row to `(src, dst, ref|None)` so a bare pair keeps working\n   and is by definition an unmapped-entry warning. All consumers (the copy pass,\n   the dogfood walk, the kit-path invariant, the resync/profile tests) unpack\n   pairs and triples.\n2. **The checker** — in `gen_arch_map.py` (LLR-204's module, the purpose-\n   reference home), the forward direction beside the backlink machinery:\n   `mapping_purpose_findings(entries, present, sr_by_id, sn_ids,\n   declared_absences)` returns the four classes; `resolve_requirement_reference`\n   is the SR → live-stakeholder-need join stated once; `load_spine_index` loads\n   the repo's SR/SN registries; `mapping_purpose_report` computes the pass.\n   `MAPPING_FINDING_POLICY` is the one home for warn-vs-gate: `unmapped_file` and\n   `unresolved_reference` WARN, `missing_file` and `stale_entry` GATE (they are\n   already delivered/zero via the dogfood+bootstrap checks). The stale arm\n   honors the `LIFECYCLE:` marker, the same rule the dogfood walk applies. The\n   flip of a warn class to gate at count zero is a later reviewed commit.\n3. **The direct TC on SR-163** — TC-204 (`tests/test_mapping_purpose.py`, Smoke\n   tier so it runs on every commit bar): plants one defect of each class on a\n   synthetic scaffold plus a clean control and asserts each is reported; drives\n   the checker over the real `bootstrap.MAPPING` + this repo's real spine and\n   asserts NO gate-class finding survives (the standing every-file-maps\n   evidence) and every filled reference resolves. Registered Drafted (SR-163 is\n   Approved; approving TC-204 is the owner's act).\n4. **Burn-down begun** — 20 references filled to unambiguous EXISTING SRs\n   (`SR-049` derived stage, `SR-137` one policy home, `SR-146` prompts ×9,\n   `SR-147` spine registries ×3, `SR-159` interfaces ×2, `SR-015` perf budgets,\n   `SR-151` hosted CI, `SR-161` hats). No new SR needed yet — no filled file\n   lacked a justifying requirement.\n\n**Baseline (recorded for the burn-down):** of 147 MAPPING rows, 20 carry a\nresolved reference and **127 remain bare (unmapped_file WARN)**; 0 unresolved, 0\nmissing, 0 stale over the real inventory. The 127 is the count the burn-down\nretires against; gating flips only at zero, per the ruling.\n\n### Design notes\n\n- No new LLR: the ruling keeps the wi508 rows (LLR-203/204, TC-199/200) as they\n  are and makes TC-204 a DIRECT test on SR-163. The checker's functions carry no\n  `Implements:` tag / LLR — back-link coverage is warn-only, and the mechanism\n  is verified by its direct TC.\n- No new `stack.ini` step: `bootstrap.py` is excluded from its own MAPPING and\n  never ships downstream, so a harness step over `bootstrap.MAPPING` would be\n  dead in every adopter. The kit self-check home is the test, which runs the\n  checker over the real inventory on every suite run — the \"on every run\"\n  evidence the ruling asks for. An adopter with their own inventory can call the\n  `gen_arch_map` functions directly.\n\n### Close\n\n- **Harness re-stamps (reviewed baseline edits naming this WI):** the checker's\n  new behavior grew two ratcheted modules past baseline — `bootstrap.py` +29\n  SLOC (1571 → 1600, the tolerant cell) and `gen_arch_map.py` +79 SLOC (1262 →\n  1341, the four-class checker) — both re-stamped UP in `tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py`\n  as reviewed bumps, not monolith drift (the placement is LLR-204's module by\n  the ruling; decomposition remains WI-521's program). TC-204's 17 in-process\n  smoke tests pushed the smoke tier to 1450 collected, so `docs/stack.ini`\n  `[smoke-budget] max-tests` re-stamped 1440 → 1458 (+8 headroom, the standing\n  small-slack posture); the seconds budget is NOT touched (smoke wall 21.8 s vs\n  60 s).\n- **Approval brief regenerated** (`trace.py --approve modified`): TC-204 (the\n  one spine row this WI minted, Drafted) now appears in `docs/ratify/CURRENT.md`\n  as ADDED-since-snapshot / never-approved — approving it is the owner's act.\n- **Verification:** commit bar green (smoke + budget enforce); the full\n  unfiltered suite run to green before close.\n","numLines":76,"startLine":1,"totalLines":76}}}
